# Friday Linux — SPEC.md §13 PR-10, §14. The only sudo rule in the image.
# Scoped to the exact binary and nothing else; the binary's own argparse
# allowlist (helper/friday-os-helper/friday-os-helper) is the second layer,
# per PR-10's acceptance criterion that a test prove this cannot be used to
# run anything else. NOPASSWD because the routes calling this run as
# User=friday inside friday.service (§8.1), which has no interactive
# terminal to prompt on.
friday ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/libexec/friday/friday-os-helper
